 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "demands lists the cars in queue order; x, y and z are the liters initially in dispensers X, Y and Z. Refuelling one liter takes one second and cars are served strictly in queue order, starting at time 0. When a car is at the front at time t it starts at the earliest time s >= t at which some dispenser holding at least its demand is free; among such dispensers free at s it takes the first of X, Y, Z. The dispenser then holds demand fewer liters and is busy until s + demand (free again at that instant), and the next car reaches the front at s. A car's waiting time is s. Return the largest waiting time over all cars (0 for no cars), or -1 when some car finds no dispenser with enough fuel left, because then the queue never empties.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk11-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
